---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ServiceLinks from '../components/ServiceLinks.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { dots } from '../lib/patterns.js';
const ask = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('An AI system for our office')}`;
const bodyBg = dots();
---
<Base title="An AI system for your office" description="I build what your office needs on a computer you own. It uses the Claude or ChatGPT account you already pay for, keeps client files off a personal chat, answers from your own documents with the page, and I train your staff.">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={5} tall mapLabel="See the system I run on" eyebrow="AI systems · Small offices" title="Built around the work you already do.">
    <p class="lede">Claude or ChatGPT can write a sentence. It has not read your files. I set up a system on a computer you own that files what comes in and answers from those files, with the page. It can use the model you already pay for. Your records stay on that computer unless you choose otherwise. Then I sit with your staff and train them on the real work. Field Agent, the phone app, shows the few things that need a person.</p>
    <a slot="actions" class="btn btn-secondary " href={ask}>Ask about your office</a>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section band-parallax">
    <div class="band-bg" set:html={bodyBg} aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every email, text, and scan read and filed where it belongs, with the noise archived and replies drafted.</li>
        <li>Your documents indexed in place, with access rules that match your office.</li>
        <li>An assistant that takes plain-English questions from your staff and shows its sources every time.</li>
        <li>Field Agent on your phone: what to answer, what is due, the next step on each job, and an Allow button before anything changes.</li>
        <li>Claude, ChatGPT, or an open-source model. If you already pay for one, this uses it. You do not buy a second subscription to make the system run.</li>
        <li>A computer you own. Your data stays on your systems unless you choose a hosted model. Staff stop pasting client files into a personal chat.</li>
        <li>A fixed-scope build, then optional monthly care for updates and new document sets.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Records still on paper or in longhand? I transcribe them first, so the system can search them. <a href="/knowledge-assistants/transcription">How transcription works</a></p>
      <p>The four steps every install follows are on the <a href="/map">system map</a>, with mine as the worked example.</p>
      <h2 id="rag">How it answers from your files: RAG</h2>
      <p>The method is called RAG, short for retrieval-augmented generation. A plain chatbot answers from what it learned on the public internet, and it can make things up. A RAG assistant first looks up the passages in your documents that match the question. Then it writes its answer from those passages and cites them. It answers from your files, and you can check every answer against the source.</p>
      <h2>Then: teach your team to use it</h2>
      <p>If the staff never use it, the account you pay for is wasted. Four weeks of training, beside them on real work, teaches them how to ask, how to check the page, and when not to trust an answer. I measure the change in your own records. <a href="/knowledge-assistants/ai-adoption">How the training works</a></p>
      <h2>Where it comes from</h2>
      <p>I run one of these for myself: a system that files my email, texts, scans, and notes into a searchable vault every day and shows me what needs me on my phone. It is the working prototype for this offer. <a href="/work#second-brain">See it on the Work page</a></p>
      <p><span class="tag">Fixed scope</span> <span class="tag">Optional monthly care</span> <span class="tag">Quote on scope</span></p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about your office</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServiceLinks current="/knowledge-assistants" />
</Base>
